arm64: dts: h713: bind the watchdog with the A523 register layout

TODO 2.25. The node said sun50i-h6-wdt/sun6i-a31-wdt, so sunxi_wdt used
CTRL +0x10, CFG +0x14, MODE +0x18 and wrote no key. On the H713 those
writes do nothing (doku/72: the pinger killed, no reset, MODE read 0x1f),
and RebootWatchdogSec armed nothing. The block has the A523's register
file - CTRL +0x0c (reload 0x14af), CFG +0x10, MODE +0x14, key 0x16aa -
which BL31 and U-Boot already use (U-Boot binds it with the same two
strings); a hand-set MODE 0x16aa00b1 resets the HY310 after 16.4 s, with
the USB cable plugged in, and a 0x14af reload on CTRL holds it off
(doku/164). sunxi_wdt knows that layout as allwinner,sun55i-a523-wdt, so
no driver change is needed for it.

The A523 binding wants both clocks by name: hosc is osc24M as before,
losc the RTC's osc32k (index 0). The driver takes neither; the interrupt
stays 53 and unrequested.

Only with a BL31 that has T1. The rootfs sets RebootWatchdogSec=16s
(mainline/tools/rootfs/customize.sh), so with this tree every reboot and
every poweroff arms the watchdog for real: systemd-shutdown starts it at
16 s, the kernel's reboot notifier stops it, and then PSCI's reset - or
the poweroff into the boot gate - programs CFG and MODE for 0.5 s. A
BL31 without T1 does that without a reload first. On the HY310 such a
MODE write into a running watchdog reset nothing, and the box stayed in
BL31 until the power was cut (crust-20261007 run B1, TFA-1; mechanism
inferred). Whether a stopped block starts again from zero is not
measured, so the stop in between does not make this safe. This holds for
test and FEL images with this rootfs as much as for the release; with
RuntimeWatchdogSec it also holds for a running watchdog.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi
@@ -1512,18 +1512,26 @@
 
 		/* === Watchdog === */
 		watchdog: watchdog@2051000 {
-			compatible = "allwinner,sun50i-h6-wdt",
-				     "allwinner,sun6i-a31-wdt";
+			/*
+			 * The A523's register file: CTRL +0x0c (reload
+			 * 0x14af), CFG +0x10, MODE +0x14, key 0x16aa - the
+			 * strings U-Boot binds it with. The H6/A31 layout
+			 * (CTRL +0x10, no key) hit nothing here (doku/72);
+			 * MODE 0x16aa00b1 resets after 16.4 s (doku/164).
+			 */
+			compatible = "allwinner,sun50i-h713-wdt",
+				     "allwinner,sun55i-a523-wdt";
 			reg = <0x02051000 0x20>;
 			/*
 			 * 53, not 46: 46 is the msgbox's bank 0 line (stock
 			 * watchdog@2051000: interrupts = <0 0x35 4>). No
-			 * behaviour change -- sun6i-a31-wdt never requests
-			 * the interrupt -- but it stops the device tree from
+			 * behaviour change -- sunxi_wdt never requests the
+			 * interrupt -- but it stops the device tree from
 			 * naming one line twice.
 			 */
 			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 53 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
-			clocks = <&osc24M>;
+			clocks = <&osc24M>, <&rtc CLK_OSC32K>;
+			clock-names = "hosc", "losc";
 		};
 
 		/* === R-domain: RTC, R_CCU, R_PIO, IR === */
